2749 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The dear CC color palette is intentionally minimal\056 As a content\055driven platform\054 the primary focus should be on ideas\054 writing\054 and clarity \024 not heavy visual styling\056 For this reason\054 the dear CC brand uses a restrained color system built around neutrals and a single accent color\056\050\nPrimary Palette\nCoral \024 Accent color\nBlack \024 Primary text and interface\nWhite \024 Background and negative space\n\050The coral accent color is used to highlight important elements such as buttons\054 links\054 key actions\054 and small brand moments\056 Black and white should make up the majority of the interface to keep the experience clean\054 readable\054 and focused on content\056\n\nWhy Only One Accent Color\050dear CC is being built quickly and iteratively\056 To maintain visual consistency while the platform evolves\054 we are intentionally limiting the brand to a single accent color for now\056 This helps the brand feel cohesive and recognizable across the website\054 social\054 presentations\054 and future product interfaces\056\nAs dear CC grows\054 the color system may expand to include additional supporting colors\056 For now\054 the restrained palette helps the brand feel clear\054 focused\054 and confident\056\n\050Usage Guide\nUse coral sparingly for emphasis and key actions\056\nUse black for the majority of text and interface elements\056\nUse white or very light backgrounds for readability\056\nAvoid introducing new colors that are not part of the core palette\056\nColor should support the content\054 not distract from it\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 2750 0 R
     /Pg 2031 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

